3.text:
The five exemplars are all C V C with

* 2nd letter ∈ {a,o,u}
* 3rd letter ∈ {b,d,t,w}

dad  d a d
dab  d a b
gut  g u t
low  l o w
cat  c a t

is the class

* 2nd ∈ {a,o,u} ∧ 3rd ∈ {b,d,t,w}

The five negative exemplars are exactly the C V C / V C V words whose
third letter is not in {b,d,t,w}

ear r , cop p , ego o , mom m , ate e .

On that reading

* leg  l e g  2nd = e ∉ {a,o,u}  3rd = g ∉ {b,d,t,w}
* dam  d a m  3rd = m ∉ {b,d,t,w}
* car  c a r  3rd = r ∉ {b,d,t,w}
* bin  b i n  2nd = i ∉ {a,o,u}  3rd = n ∉ {b,d,t,w}

are all non-members of the class.  The only member of the set
{A–E} that does satisfy 2nd∈{a,o,u}∧3rd∈{b,d,t,w} is

C. rat  r a t

i.e. r a t is the only option that is of the same C V C type as
dad/dab/gut/low/cat.  In particular leg is a textbook non-member:
l e g is C V C but 2nd=e and 3rd=g are both outside the pattern sets,
so it is of the ear/cop/ego/mom/ate type.  The same is true, mutatis
mutandis, of dam, car and bin.

